name: sim.insertObjectIntoOctree
description: Inserts an object into an OC tree, as voxels. Each voxel will store a color and a tag value
luaSynopsis: int totalVoxelCnt = sim.insertObjectIntoOctree(int octreeHandle, int objectHandle, int options, list color = None, int tag = 0)
pythonSynopsis: int totalVoxelCnt = sim.insertObjectIntoOctree(int octreeHandle, int objectHandle, int options, int[] color = nil, int tag = 0)
inputs:
1. octreeHandle: handle of the OC tree
2. objectHandle: handle of the object to insert. Only potentially collidable objects are supported
3. options: reserved. Set to 0
4. color: array of RGB triplet, specifying the red, green and blue color components (0 - 255). Can be None/nil
5. tag: uint32 value, which is user-defined
outputs:
1. totalVoxelCnt: the total number of voxels in the OC tree
replacedBy:
- name: addFromObjects, class: ocTree, file: ocTree_addFromObjects.method
